		{
			"to": "feynman/character-of-law",
			"why": "Feynman's lost lecture began from Kepler's second law, equal areas in equal times, and derived the ellipse Kepler found in Tycho's figures for Mars from an inverse-square force."
		},
		{
			"to": "physics/ptolemy",
			"why": "Kepler's ellipses in the Astronomia nova of 1609 wholly replaced Ptolemy's circles, and the empty focus stands about where Ptolemy put the equant."
		},
		{
			"to": "physics/copernicus",
			"why": "Kepler kept Copernicus's Sun at the centre but replaced the circles and epicycles Copernicus had kept with ellipses."
